I found two concrete issues. LPP I Theorem 1.3 uses \(h\ge x^{3/5}\) and the density loss \(\exp[-(\log x)^{1/3}(\log\log x)^{8/3}]\); the note misquotes both exponents, though its unconditional conclusion survives. Also, Soundararajan’s 2010 weighted estimate combined with classical divisor-moment bounds gives an \(L[1/2]\)-scale density lower bound. That weakens the claimed dependence on Younis for novelty.

