   428	  - Conjecture (2.10) gives the conditional L_p[1/2, √2].
   429	  - Lenstra notes that under GRH Prop (2.7) improves by a log log p factor. That is an
   430	    L^{o(1)} effect.
   431	- **Younis 2024**: Thms 1.1–1.3. The paper names no application to factoring.
   432	- **Soundararajan 2010** (arXiv:1009.1591; RH): existence in [x, x + C(ε)√x] for y = x^ε,
   433	  and the lower bound z x^{−ε} above. It says explicitly that this is "still not strong enough
   434	  to be applicable to the analysis of Lenstra's algorithm".
   435	- **Granville 2008 survey** ("Smooth numbers: computational number theory and beyond"), §4a:
   436	  pre-2024 short-interval results.
   437	  - Friedlander–Granville 1993: asymptotic for y ≥ exp((log x)^{5/6+o(1)}),
   438	    √x y² exp((log x)^{1/6}) ≤ z ≤ x.
   439	  - Harman 1991 and LPP 1993: lower bounds for y ≥ exp((log x)^{2/3+o(1)}).
   440	  - Xuan 1999 (RH): existence in [x, x + √x (log x)^{1+o(1)}] for y = x^ε.
   441	  - Hafner 1993 (RH, unpublished, an "almost all intervals" result per Soundararajan).
   442	  - None gives, before 2024, an RH density lower bound at y = L[1/2] for intervals x^θ with
